# LF everywhere, in the index AND in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The first version of this file pinned only packages/tickets/schemas/*.json,
# because that is the artifact whose drift gate went red on the Windows leg of
# the ticket-store matrix: git hands that leg CRLF, the byte comparison against
# the generator sees every line differ, and `npm pack` from such a checkout
# would ship a schema whose bytes are not the generated ones.
#
# That scope was too narrow — it fixes one artifact and leaves the NEXT
# generated file someone byte-compares to rediscover the same bug (cross-model
# review, MEDIUM). Repo-wide costs nothing HERE, and that was measured rather
# than assumed: under this file `git add --renormalize .` rewrites zero tracked
# files, no tracked file contains a CR byte, and the repo has no .bat/.cmd/.ps1
# that would want CRLF. `text=auto` still auto-detects binary, so images and
# archives are left alone.
#
# KNOWN LIMIT: git does not retroactively renormalize a working tree that already
# exists. CI clones fresh, so it is unaffected; a Windows contributor with an
# older checkout runs `git add --renormalize .` once.
* text=auto eol=lf
